## Context
The current spec-erg-v1.md conflates two concerns: the file format (stable,
binary-independent) and the command reference (changes with the code). The
command sections are already partially written as Go doc comments in the source
— they should be the single source of truth, serving as per-command --help,
as a full --help --all manual, and as a generated static artifact.

## Child tickets
- 0089: Enrich Go doc comments with spec command sections
- 0090: Serve per-command --help text from doc comments
- 0091: Add erg --help --all and make docs target
- 0092: Cull spec-erg-v1.md to file-format sections only

## Exit criteria
- [ ] All four child tickets closed
- [ ] `erg COMMAND --help` prints rich per-command documentation
- [ ] `erg --help --all` prints the full manual
- [ ] `make docs` generates erg-manual.md from the binary
- [ ] spec-erg-v1.md covers file format only (≤150 lines)
- [ ] No content duplication between spec and binary help
